title: Exact ERC-20 transfers and revert reasons in the assets and asset-conversion precompiles

doc:
- audience: Runtime Dev
  description: |-
    The assets ERC-20 precompile now reverts a `transfer` or `transferFrom` that would leave the
    sender a non-zero balance below `min_balance`, instead of letting pallet-assets sweep the
    remainder to the recipient. `pallet-assets` is unchanged.

    Pallet errors from both precompiles now revert with the `DispatchError` reason, which is the
    variant name for module errors. A state change under `STATICCALL` still fails with no return
    data.

    `pallet-asset-conversion` adds `Pallet::pool_exists` and `WeightInfo::pool_exists`, used by
    the precompile to tell a missing pool from an empty one. Its swap `withdraw` refuses a credit
    that differs from the requested amount.

- audience: Runtime User
  description: |-
    ERC-20 `transfer` and `transferFrom` on pallet-assets tokens revert with "Transfer would leave
    sender below minimum balance" rather than sending more than `value`. Send the full balance or
    keep at least the minimum. A contract that tracks deposits should pay out `balanceOf(this)` on
    the last withdrawal, since anyone can send it a small amount that puts the tracked total in
    that range.

    Precompile reverts now use error names such as "AssetNotLive" or "PoolEmpty". Quotes report
    "Amount can't be zero", "Pool does not exist", "Pool exists but has no liquidity" or
    "Quote failed".

crates:
- name: pallet-asset-conversion
  bump: major
- name: pallet-assets-precompiles
  bump: patch
- name: pallet-asset-conversion-precompiles
  bump: patch
- name: pallet-revive
  bump: none
- name: asset-hub-westend-runtime
  bump: patch
- name: asset-hub-rococo-runtime
  bump: patch
- name: pallet-staking-async-parachain-runtime
  bump: patch
